{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014c7QpHEJmUYR5t1K6Bx3Xd","type":"tool_result","content":"740\t            zc_result: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n741\t            logup_result: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n742\t        }\n743\t\n744\t        // Phase 1: Launch all GPU kernels without blocking D2H transfers.\n745\t        // Collect result buffers and metadata for Phase 2 processing.\n746\t        let mut pending: Vec<Round0Pending<F, EF>> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\n747\t        // Collect d_main_parts to keep them alive until all kernels complete.\n748\t        let mut d_main_parts_vec: Vec<DeviceBuffer<*const F>> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\n749\t\n750\t        for (trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, selectors_cube, public_values, eq_3bs)) in izip!(\n751\t            &ctx.per_trace,\n752\t            &self.n_per_trace,\n753\t            &selectors_base,\n754\t            &self.public_values_per_trace,\n755\t            &self.eq_3b_per_trace,\n756\t        )\n757\t        .enumerate()\n758\t        {\n759\t            debug!(\"starting batch constraints for air_idx={air_idx} (trace_idx={trace_idx})\");\n760\t            let single_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n761\t            // Includes both plain AIR constraints and symbolic interactions\n762\t            let single_air_constraints =\n763\t                SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n764\t            let local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n765\t            debug_assert_eq!(\n766\t                single_air_constraints.max_constraint_degree(),\n767\t                local_constraint_deg\n768\t            );\n769\t            assert!(\n770\t                local_constraint_deg <= self.constraint_degree,\n771\t                \"Max constraint degree ({local_constraint_deg}) of AIR {air_idx} exceeds the global maximum {}\",\n772\t                self.constraint_degree\n773\t            );\n774\t\n775\t            let log_large_domain = log2_ceil_usize(local_constraint_deg << l_skip);\n776\t            let omega_root = F::two_adic_generator(log_large_domain);\n777\t\n778\t            assert!(!xi.is_empty(), \"xi vector must not be empty\");\n779\t\n780\t            let height = air_ctx.common_main.height();\n781\t            let mut main_parts = Vec::with_capacity(air_ctx.cached_mains.len() + 1);\n782\t            for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains {\n783\t                main_parts.push(committed.trace.buffer().as_ptr());\n784\t            }\n785\t            main_parts.push(air_ctx.common_main.buffer().as_ptr());\n786\t            let d_main_parts = main_parts.to_device()?;\n787\t\n788\t            let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n789\t            let eq_xi_tree = &self.eq_xis[&n_lift];\n790\t            let max_temp_bytes = self.memory_limit_bytes;\n791\t            // local_constraint_deg = 0 means no constraints. The only way that linear constraints\n792\t            // on trace polynomials could vanish on 2^l_skip points is if the constraint polynomial\n793\t            // is identically zero. Thus for local_constraint_deg = 0 or 1, we must have `s'_0 = 0`.\n794\t            let num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n795\t            let zc_result = evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(\n796\t                single_pk,\n797\t                selectors_cube.buffer(),\n798\t                &d_main_parts,\n799\t                public_values,\n800\t                eq_xi_tree.get_ptr(n_lift),\n801\t                d_lambda_pows,\n802\t                1 << l_skip,\n803\t                1 << n_lift,\n804\t                height as u32,\n805\t                num_cosets_zc as u32,\n806\t                omega_root,\n807\t                max_temp_bytes,\n808\t            )?;\n809\t\n810\t            // PERF: we could use an interaction-specific constraint degree here\n811\t            let num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg;\n812\t            let logup_result = evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu(\n813\t                single_pk,\n814\t                &single_air_constraints,\n815\t                selectors_cube.buffer(),\n816\t                &d_main_parts,\n817\t                public_values,\n818\t                eq_xi_tree.get_ptr(n_lift),\n819\t                &self.beta_pows,\n820\t                eq_3bs,\n821\t                1 << l_skip,\n822\t                1 << n_lift,\n823\t                height as u32,\n824\t                num_cosets_logup as u32,\n825\t                omega_root,\n826\t                max_temp_bytes,\n827\t            )?;\n828\t\n829\t            d_main_parts_vec.push(d_main_parts);\n830\t            pending.push(Round0Pending {\n831\t                trace_idx,\n832\t                air_idx: *air_idx,\n833\t                num_cosets_zc,\n834\t                num_cosets_logup,\n835\t                local_constraint_deg,\n836\t                omega_root,\n837\t                n,\n838\t                zc_result,\n839\t                logup_result,\n840\t            });\n841\t        }\n842\t\n843\t        // Phase 2: Explicit stream sync, then D2H transfers + CPU polynomial construction.\n844\t        current_stream_sync().map_err(|e| LogupZerocheckError::from(MemCopyError::from(e)))?;\n845\t\n846\t        // Release d_main_parts now that all kernels have completed\n847\t        drop(d_main_parts_vec);\n848\t\n849\t        for entry in pending {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1de075eb-7395-4d25-b825-c548ab1430ba","uuid":"f313e30a-b5f0-4d9a-b1e5-d942ea311a4d","timestamp":"2026-04-11T08:29:24.573Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs","content":"            zc_result: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n            logup_result: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n        }\n\n        // Phase 1: Launch all GPU kernels without blocking D2H transfers.\n        // Collect result buffers and metadata for Phase 2 processing.\n        let mut pending: Vec<Round0Pending<F, EF>> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\n        // Collect d_main_parts to keep them alive until all kernels complete.\n        let mut d_main_parts_vec: Vec<DeviceBuffer<*const F>> = Vec::with_capacity(num_present_airs);\n\n        for (trace_idx, ((air_idx, air_ctx), &n, selectors_cube, public_values, eq_3bs)) in izip!(\n            &ctx.per_trace,\n            &self.n_per_trace,\n            &selectors_base,\n            &self.public_values_per_trace,\n            &self.eq_3b_per_trace,\n        )\n        .enumerate()\n        {\n            debug!(\"starting batch constraints for air_idx={air_idx} (trace_idx={trace_idx})\");\n            let single_pk = &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx];\n            // Includes both plain AIR constraints and symbolic interactions\n            let single_air_constraints =\n                SymbolicConstraints::from(&single_pk.vk.symbolic_constraints);\n            let local_constraint_deg = single_pk.vk.max_constraint_degree as usize;\n            debug_assert_eq!(\n                single_air_constraints.max_constraint_degree(),\n                local_constraint_deg\n            );\n            assert!(\n                local_constraint_deg <= self.constraint_degree,\n                \"Max constraint degree ({local_constraint_deg}) of AIR {air_idx} exceeds the global maximum {}\",\n                self.constraint_degree\n            );\n\n            let log_large_domain = log2_ceil_usize(local_constraint_deg << l_skip);\n            let omega_root = F::two_adic_generator(log_large_domain);\n\n            assert!(!xi.is_empty(), \"xi vector must not be empty\");\n\n            let height = air_ctx.common_main.height();\n            let mut main_parts = Vec::with_capacity(air_ctx.cached_mains.len() + 1);\n            for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains {\n                main_parts.push(committed.trace.buffer().as_ptr());\n            }\n            main_parts.push(air_ctx.common_main.buffer().as_ptr());\n            let d_main_parts = main_parts.to_device()?;\n\n            let n_lift = n.max(0) as usize;\n            let eq_xi_tree = &self.eq_xis[&n_lift];\n            let max_temp_bytes = self.memory_limit_bytes;\n            // local_constraint_deg = 0 means no constraints. The only way that linear constraints\n            // on trace polynomials could vanish on 2^l_skip points is if the constraint polynomial\n            // is identically zero. Thus for local_constraint_deg = 0 or 1, we must have `s'_0 = 0`.\n            let num_cosets_zc = local_constraint_deg.saturating_sub(1);\n            let zc_result = evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu(\n                single_pk,\n                selectors_cube.buffer(),\n                &d_main_parts,\n                public_values,\n                eq_xi_tree.get_ptr(n_lift),\n                d_lambda_pows,\n                1 << l_skip,\n                1 << n_lift,\n                height as u32,\n                num_cosets_zc as u32,\n                omega_root,\n                max_temp_bytes,\n            )?;\n\n            // PERF: we could use an interaction-specific constraint degree here\n            let num_cosets_logup = local_constraint_deg;\n            let logup_result = evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu(\n                single_pk,\n                &single_air_constraints,\n                selectors_cube.buffer(),\n                &d_main_parts,\n                public_values,\n                eq_xi_tree.get_ptr(n_lift),\n                &self.beta_pows,\n                eq_3bs,\n                1 << l_skip,\n                1 << n_lift,\n                height as u32,\n                num_cosets_logup as u32,\n                omega_root,\n                max_temp_bytes,\n            )?;\n\n            d_main_parts_vec.push(d_main_parts);\n            pending.push(Round0Pending {\n                trace_idx,\n                air_idx: *air_idx,\n                num_cosets_zc,\n                num_cosets_logup,\n                local_constraint_deg,\n                omega_root,\n                n,\n                zc_result,\n                logup_result,\n            });\n        }\n\n        // Phase 2: Explicit stream sync, then D2H transfers + CPU polynomial construction.\n        current_stream_sync().map_err(|e| LogupZerocheckError::from(MemCopyError::from(e)))?;\n\n        // Release d_main_parts now that all kernels have completed\n        drop(d_main_parts_vec);\n\n        for entry in pending {","numLines":110,"startLine":740,"totalLines":1649}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012jQvKfj1rxhcxAc5VcJpnL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear understanding of the current Round 0 implementation:\n\n1. Phase 1 iterates sequentially over all AIR instances (750-841)\n2. For each AIR:\n   - Constructs `SymbolicConstraints` from the proving key\n   - Calculates NTT parameters (log_large_domain, omega_root, etc.)\n   - Sets up main_parts pointers and H2D transfers them\n   - Launches `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` (zerocheck) \n   - Launches `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (logup)\n   - Stores result buffers in pending vec\n3. Phase 2 syncs and processes results\n\nThe key insight: `skip_domain = 1 << l_skip` and `num_x = 1 << n_lift`. For small AIRs (autoprecompiles), `n_lift` might be small (e.g., 8-12, meaning 256-4096 rows), and `l_skip` is determined by the global constraint degree. The memory bottleneck from the previous batch attempt came down to how the temp buffer scales per AIR in the batched kernel.\n\nFor each AIR in the batch, I need separate intermediates and temp_sums, with output size scaling as `num_cosets * skip_domain`. With `l_skip = 13` and `num_cosets = 2`, a single AIR produces 256KB of output, so 32 AIRs fit comfortably in 8MB. However, larger AIRs with `l_skip` values above 20 would blow up the output buffer, though those wouldn't typically be coset-parallel anyway.\n\nThe key insight is that coset-parallel candidates should all have manageable memory footprints. The previous OOM likely came from batching AIRs with different `skip_domain` sizes and padding everything to the maximum. I should group AIRs by compatible `skip_domain` and `num_cosets` values to eliminate padding waste, cap the batch size to stay within memory limits, and launch each batch as a single kernel. This approach should handle the pairing benchmark well.\n\nCompiling the performance data now... Looking at the performance breakdown for the stacked reduction and trace commit phases, then examining the scaling ratio which shows a 1.031x increase from APC 0 to APC 300 — notably better than the baseline 1.153x. Now I'm diving into the kernel-level profiling for Round 0, analyzing the coset-parallel launches across different SHMEM configurations and their utilization patterns.\n\nI'm identifying three main optimization opportunities: sub-batching the Round 0 coset-parallel kernels could save 200-350ms with medium-high confidence since similar CUDA optimizations have worked before, batching the LogUp GKR input evaluation kernels might recover 100-200ms with moderate confidence, and optimizing the zero hash calculation in Trace Commit could yield 50-80ms with high confidence but minimal complexity.\n\nLooking at the remaining options, pre-allocating device buffers offers a quick 20-30ms win with high probability, while multi-stream execution could theoretically save 200-400ms but requires substantial infrastructure changes and has low confidence. The first option stands out as the best trade-off between expected gains and implementation difficulty, so I'll focus on that approach and document the findings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1719,"cache_read_input_tokens":94853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1719},"output_tokens":12,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1de075eb-7395-4d25-b825-c548ab1430ba","uuid":"17393c99-b5f5-46a3-ae2e-cf9d7cc459d3"}
